---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Methods · Recovery Observatory">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Methods</p>
      <h1>From event boundary to recovery trajectory.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The observatory is designed around reproducible spatial comparison:
        define the disaster geography, normalize indicators, trace temporal
        change, and interpret recovery through ecological, socioeconomic,
        demographic, social, and policy evidence.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid two">
        <article class="card"><h3>Spatial Frame</h3><p>Establish a disaster boundary, affected administrative units, and comparable spatial grids or zones.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Temporal Frame</h3><p>Store annual or milestone observations to distinguish emergency response, reconstruction, stabilization, and long-run transformation.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Indicator Harmonization</h3><p>Keep raw data transparent, then derive comparable measures using consistent units, time windows, spatial aggregation, and uncertainty notes.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Mixed Evidence</h3><p>Combine remote sensing, census and statistical data, policy texts, news, social media, planning documents, field observations, and interviews when available.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Reproducible Pipeline</p>
          <h2>Every value needs a source trail.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Fetch scripts write provenance logs first. The processing script then
          turns those logs into chart-ready files and keeps missing geospatial
          layers marked as <code>manual_required</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid three">
        <article class="card"><h3>Fetch</h3><p><code>scripts/fetch_usgs.py</code>, <code>fetch_reliefweb.py</code>, and <code>fetch_worldbank.py</code> collect API responses and access notes under <code>public/data/provenance/</code>.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Process</h3><p><code>scripts/process_all.py</code> standardizes event metadata, national context indicators, report frequency, and documented data gaps into <code>public/data/processed/</code>.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Review</h3><p>Remote-sensing layers remain documented placeholders until boundary selection, raster download, masking, and zonal statistics are completed reproducibly.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
